action                   List, view, run, export, apply and delete actions
  apply                  Create or update an action from a definition file
  delete <action>        Delete an action
  example                Print an example definition with every option
  export <action>        Print the definition of an action as YAML
  list                   List actions
  run <action>           Run an action on servers and follow it live
  view <action>          View the steps and variables of an action
api <method> <path>      Send an authenticated request to the REST API and print the JSON
completion <shell>       Print the shell completion script (bash, zsh, fish, powershell)
env                      Add, list and switch the configured environments (instances)
  add [name]             Add an environment: an instance with your API token for it
  list                   List the environments, the active one marked
  use <environment>      Make an environment the active one for all following commands
pipe                     List and view pipes (automations)
  list                   List pipes
  view <pipe>            View the trigger and steps of a pipe
run                      List, view, watch and cancel runs
  cancel <run>           Cancel a run: terminate it on all servers
  list                   List the latest runs
  view <run>             View a run with its steps, or its full log with --log
  watch <run>            Follow a run live until it finishes
server                   List and view servers, their health and connections
  connect <server>       Open the SSH connection of a server
  disconnect <server>    Close the SSH connection of a server
  list                   List servers with CPU, memory, disk and load
  view <server>          View the dashboard of a server: system, usage and latest runs
status                   Check the configuration, the API token and the real-time gateway
team                     List and view your teams, limit all commands to one of them
  list                   List your teams
  use <team>             Limit all following commands to a team, or --all for all teams
  view <team>            View the members of a team
template                 List, view, export, apply and delete file templates
  apply                  Create or update a template from a definition file
  delete <template>      Delete a template
  example                Print an example definition with every option
  export <template>      Print the definition of a template as YAML
  list                   List templates
  view <template>        View the content of a template
terminal                 List, open and join shared terminal sessions
  join <session>         Join a running terminal session of your team
  list                   List the running terminal sessions of your teams
  open <server>          Open a shared terminal session on a server
update                   Update pt to the latest version
variable                 List the variables of your account, a team or a server
  list                   List the variables of your account, or of a server or team
version                  Print the version of pt
workflow                 List, view, run, export, apply and delete workflows
  apply                  Create or update a workflow from a definition file
  delete <workflow>      Delete a workflow
  example                Print an example definition with every option
  export <workflow>      Print the definition of a workflow as YAML
  list                   List workflows
  run <workflow>         Run a workflow on servers and follow it live
  view <workflow>        View the steps and variables of a workflow
